Excitation_Wavelength(nm)":525,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1002/anie.202202098","Year":2022,"Counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-023659","value":"16.5","numeric":16.5}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-023660","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"Ir1","Cell_line":"NP69","Time(h)":48,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":21.7,"IC50_Dark_value":21.7,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1002/anie.202202098","Year":2022,"Counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","Type":"IC50"}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"Ir1","value":0.13,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1002/anie.202202098","year":2022,"counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-000029","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"Mixture of n-octanol and water (1:1 v/v, 20 mL) was shook for 24 h by a constant temperature oscillator so that the two phases can be saturated with each other. Then, the two-phase distribution was carried out. The Ir1-Ir2 were added to a mixture of 1 mL water-saturated n-octanol and 1 mL n-octanol saturated water to obtain the final concentration of 50 μM. The solution was mixed and then vortexed on a constant temperature oscillator for overnight. After stationary, the two-phases were dispersed in 2 mL ethanol, respectively, and then the complex concentration in each phase was quantified by measuring the absorbance at 465 nm. The calculation formula: Log P = the concentration of complex in n-octanol phase/the concentration of complex in water phase."}]}